WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:34.534
OFFICER: There's tampering here.
Refer to secondary.

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:47.088
IGLESIAS: This vehicle came
from primary and right now

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.215
we're gonna do an
inspection on the vehicle.

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:51.301
The passenger is coming
from Reynosa where he lives.

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:53.053
He's going to work.

00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:55.096
The subject right now is
claiming that he's in a hurry.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:57.057
That's usually a
red flag on us.

00:00:57.098 --> 00:00:59.100
Trying to
pressure our inspection.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:02.020
So we're gonna see
what is in the vehicle.

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:06.274
We usually start from the front
and work ourselves around.

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:16.367
There's nothing here.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:19.746
We usually tap to see if
there's any, uh, if there's

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:21.748
a solid feeling or
something like that.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.124
That might be an indicator
that something might

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:24.709
be in there.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.462
We'll check the back seats.

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:32.217
See if there's anything here.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:36.304
We see for any, any tampering,
anything like that.

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:39.099
Tampering means they removed
something and usually those

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.477
are, uh, indicators of there
being something in the vehicle.

00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:51.653
And you can see
there's tampering here.

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:53.822
There's bolts here.

00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:56.324
Those are factory but
they have been removed.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:57.826
That's an indicator
there's might be

00:01:57.826 --> 00:01:59.828
something in the vehicle.

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:01.538
We're gonna continue
checking on the vehicle,

00:02:01.579 --> 00:02:03.581
if there's any additional
tampering on the car.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.291
That's already a red
flag on the vehicle.

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:08.044
There's probably gonna
be something in there.

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:12.173
The bolts have been scuffed,
like, they had been hit with a

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:14.342
ratchet or
something like that.

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:17.554
That's usually a red flag, the,
the seat has been removed.

00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:20.682
That's not normal on a vehicle
to have a seat removed.

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:23.518
But right now we're gonna
call our, uh, K9 officer.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.645
K9 OFFICER: Hey, ready?

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.712
That's a good alert.

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:54.549
Good boy.
Good boy.

00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:56.259
You've got a positive alert.

00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:57.385
Secure the subject.

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:58.636
OFFICER: 10-4.

